hundreds of passengers on board a United  Airlines flight were left trapped on the  tarmac in Canada for more than 15 hours  flight 179 left Newark New Jersey headed  to Hong Kong on Saturday 250 passengers  and 15 crew were on board about three  hours into the flight the plane was  diverted to Newfoundland after a  passenger had a medical emergency the  passenger was taken to the hospital but  before the plane could take off one of  the emergency doors malfunctioned in the  freezing temperatures it happened to be  minus 25 with minus 65 degree windchill  so with no customs borders officers  working overnight passengers were forced  to spend the night on the plane the  plane had heat but only limited snacks  the choice of airport I think was very  poor  since you know Airport was not equipped  I think everybody understood that there  was a circumstance that said nobody  could really control second United  Airlines plane landed in Canada around  noon on Sunday and brought the stranded  passengers back to Newark they arrived  last night about 27 hours after their  original departure United has apologized  and offered the customers refunds  compensation and hotel accommodations  headache for them
 

